{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDPUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDPUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRealUniqueness","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_T_w_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_T_w_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CanonicalKnotIdSDPUniqueness.lean#L129-L144","doc":"**Subsingleton form** — typeclass-friendly version of the\nabove, suitable for use as `[Subsingleton …]` instance argument\ndownstream. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_T_w_unique_under_strict_complementarity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_T_w_unique_under_strict_complementarity","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CanonicalKnotIdSDPUniqueness.lean#L104-L127","doc":"**Canonical T_w uniqueness** — Hecke-algebra-flavoured\nspecialisation of `strict_complementarity_unique`.  Given an\nSDP whose primal optimum is the cast of a Hecke element\n`T_w_star`, any other primal-feasible Hecke element with the\nsame objective value casts to the same matrix — and (in the\nfull theory) is therefore equal to `T_w_star`.\n\nThis is the bridge theorem the `conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean`\n`helium3_canonical_uniqueness_via_strict_complementarity` will\nconsume once the per-nucleus SDP instance and certificate are\nconstructed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeAsMatrix_posSemidef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeAsMatrix_posSemidef","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CanonicalKnotIdSDPUniqueness.lean#L57-L102","doc":"**Hecke-element-as-PSD-matrix** is positive-semidefinite —\nrank-1 outer products always are.\n\nPROOF: write `heckeAsMatrix x = (col x) · (col x)ᵀ`.  Then\napply Mathlib's `Matrix.posSemidef_self_mul_transpose` (or\nsimilar — verify exact name).  Direct unfolding works:\n`((col x) · (col x)ᵀ) i j = Σ_k (col x) i k · ((col x)ᵀ) k j\n= (col x) i 0 · (col x) j 0 = x i · x j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeAsMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeAsMatrix","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CanonicalKnotIdSDPUniqueness.lean#L46-L55","doc":"**Hecke element → matrix representation** stub.  Casts an\nabstract `HeckeElement n` into a matrix in the dimension\nexpected by `SDPPrimal`.  Concrete representation: the\nrank-1 outer product `x ⊗ x`, which is positive-semidefinite\nfor ALL `x` (including `x = 0`, where the result is the zero\nmatrix; PSD by convention).  The full Wedderburn-block\nrepresentation is the open Lean port of Hoefsmit. ","signatureChunk":0}]}